tecture Viewpoints (Catalogs, Matrices, Diagrams in Mermaid). The Baseline must reconcile TWO evidence sources: the session knowledge graph (claimed/narrated architecture) and the Tree-sitter code graph (observed architecture), citing CORRELATES_WITH links where claims and code agree and flagging where they diverge.\"\n  },\n  \"plan\": {\n    \"tasks\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"sad_planning\",\n        \"description\": \"Planner Agent: Decompose focus topic '${topic}' into a structured TOGAF-compliant System Architecture Document outline targeting a length of ${word_count_target} words. Scope context, identify stakeholders, baseline, target states, and draft the Scope and Context section of the report. Note the dual-evidence method: the workspace graph holds BOTH a session knowledge graph (Source/Concept nodes from LONGVIEW synthesis) and a code graph (File/Class/Function nodes from a Tree-sitter scan of the prime-silo repo), linked by CORRELATES_WITH edges.\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"planner\",\n        \"dependencies\": [],\n        \"wave\": 0,\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"node_type\": \"task\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"baseline_extraction\",\n        \"description\": \"Current State Analyst: Document the Baseline Application Architecture (Current State) of '${topic}' from BOTH graphs via `query_graph`. (1) OBSERVED architecture from the code graph: `MATCH (f:File) RETURN f.path LIMIT 200` for the file inventory; `MATCH (c:Class) RETURN c.name, c.file LIMIT 100` and `MATCH (fn:Function) RETURN fn.name, fn.file LIMIT 150` for the symbol catalog; `MATCH (a)-[r:DEPENDS_ON]->(b) RETURN a.name, b.name LIMIT 150` for dependencies. Group Folder/File paths into applications (app/=frontend, server/=API server, runtime/benny/=Benny runtime, commands/=CLI, scripts/=pipelines, packaging/=desktop shell). (2) CLAIMED architecture from the knowledge graph: `MATCH (c:Concept)-[:RELATES_TO]-(d:Concept) RETURN c.name, d.name LIMIT 150` and `search_kb` for narrative context. (3) RECONCILIATION: `MATCH (c:Concept)-[r:CORRELATES_WITH]-(code) RETURN c.name, code.name, r.confidence ORDER BY r.confidence DESC LIMIT 100` — where sessions and code agree, cite it; where a claimed capability has NO code correlate, flag it explicitly as unverified. Compile the Application Portfolio Catalog and Interface Catalog from this evidence.\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"document_analyst\",\n        \"assigned_skills\": [\"query_graph\", \"read_file\", \"search_kb\"],\n        \"dependencies\": [\"sad_planning\"],\n        \"wave\": 1,\n        \"complexity\": \"high\",\n        \"node_type\": \"task\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"target_abstraction\",\n        \"description\": \"Target State Architect: Define the Target Application Architecture (Future State) for the system '${topic}'. Explicitly distinguish between Logical Application Components (abstraction of functionality independent of implementation) and Physical Application Components (actual deployed software/services — ground these in the code-graph file inventory from the baseline). Define key meta-model relationships: realizes (Component to Service), supports (Service to Process), consumes (Actor/Role to Service), accesses/updates (Component to Data Entity), communicates with (Component to Component), and hosts (Technology to Component).\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"architect\",\n        \"dependencies\": [\"baseline_extraction\"],\n        \"wave\": 2,\n        \"complexity\": \"high\",\n        \"node_type\": \"task\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"gap_and_impact_analysis\",\n        \"description\": \"Delta Analyst: Analyze the delta between baseline and target states. Explicitly identify components to be created, updated, or decommissioned (Gap Analysis). Include a claimed-vs-observed gap class: capabilities the session knowledge graph asserts but the code graph does not corroborate (and vice versa — code with no narrated purpose). Perform Impact Analysis detailing security, downstream reporting, and infrastructure impacts.\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"analyst\",\n        \"dependencies\": [\"target_abstraction\"],\n        \"wave\": 3,\n        \"complexity\": \"high\",\n        \"node_type\": \"task\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"viewpoints_generation\",\n        \"description\": \"Viewpoint Designer: Formulate architectural viewpoints. Generate Catalogs and Matrices (Application/Business Function Matrix, Application/Data Matrix). Write out Diagrams (Application Communication Diagram, Application and User Location Diagram, Enterprise Manageability Diagram) using Mermaid syntax. Base the Application Communication Diagram on the DEPENDS_ON edges observed in the code graph.\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"designer\",\n        \"dependencies\": [\"gap_and_impact_analysis\"],\n        \"wave\": 4,\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"node_type\": \"task\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"editorial_refinement\",\n        \"description\": \"Publishing Editor: Refine the combined draft section-by-section using sliding window constraints to ensure consistency, tone, and that the final output satisfies the target length of ${word_count_target} words. Write the final TOGAF-compliant System Architecture Document (SAD) to '${output_file}'.\",\n        \"assigned_model\": \"${model}\",\n        \"persona\": \"editor\",\n        \"assigned_skills\": [\"read_file\", \"write_file\"],\n        \"dependencies\": [\"viewpoints_generation\"],\n        \"wave\": 5,\n        \"complexity\": \"high\",\n        \"node_type\": \"output\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"edges\": [\n      [\"sad_planning\", \"baseline_extraction\"],\n      [\"baseline_extraction\", \"target_abstraction\"],\n      [\"target_abstraction\", \"gap_and_impact_analysis\"],\n      [\"gap_and_impact_analysis\", \"viewpoints_generation\"],\n      [\"viewpoints_generation\", \"editorial_refinement\"]\n    ],\n    \"waves\": [\n      [\"sad_planning\"],\n      [\"baseline_extraction\"],\n      [\"target_abstraction\"],\n      [\"gap_and_impact_analysis\"],\n      [\"viewpoints_generation\"],\n      [\"editorial_refinement\"]\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"publishing_standard\": \"TOGAF-SAD-Standard\",\n    \"notes\": \"Dual-graph TOGAF SAD for the binary16 estate. Prerequisites: (1) Neo4j up; (2) `benny enrich --workspace sessions_v1 --src src/prime-silo --run` completed so the code graph + CORRELATES_WITH overlay exist alongside the LONGVIEW KG. Human-launched per ADR-001. Additive copy of togaf_sad_report_swarm.json — the original template is untouched.\"\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":108822,"output_tokens":3274,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3274,"cache_read_input_tokens":108822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cd5sBWTLv5FXApKUrtCbd","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c486f2a-0177-4042-8d85-6fc061bdb469","timestamp":"2026-07-16T14:07:29.068Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime","sessionId":"819e8a27-efc3-4128-b1f7-aa2f2dc4c806","version":"2.1.209","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
