tion register to list which models have actually been used.\n\nThen I'm generating a suite of diagrams from the codebase itself — C4 diagrams from the repo structure, ER diagrams queried directly from the Neo4j schema, class diagrams showing the top methods, sequence diagrams from actual run events, deployment topology from docker-compose and provider configs, and use-case flows from the manifest personas.\n\nFor the data model, I'm capturing it at three levels: the conceptual ontology from Neo4j labels, the logical schema with properties per label, and the physical storage layer across RocksDB, Neo4j, Chroma, and files on disk.\n\nThen Phase B runs the existing enterprise manifest through the swarm to generate narrative sections with harvested evidence woven into the task descriptions, and Phase C assembles everything into one epic markdown document with the TOC, narrative, evidence, all diagrams, and observability lineage.\n\nFor observability, I'm having the CLI emit governance events directly through the audit module so the dashboard picks up live progress—the swarm part already has dashboarding, and I can emit task metadata updates from the CLI for full transparency on each phase step-through.\n\nNow I need to look at the existing enterprise templates to use as a baseline for improving the manifest, then decide whether to build the autonomous execution right away since the user wants a testable CLI script.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308934,"cache_read_input_tokens":24222,"output_tokens":2468,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":308934,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2468,"cache_read_input_tokens":24222,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_in