{"parentUuid":"be486364-53d0-4e58-b28e-e3f859c3f3c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cd7MMt3AYBa39MaESxWtP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've got a solid hardware setup to work with: an AMD Ryzen AI 7 350 with an XDNA NPU and Radeon 860M iGPU on the local machine, plus 31GB of RAM. The eGPU with 16GB VRAM is on a separate LAN box, which sets up a perfect comparison between running lightweight models locally on the NPU versus offloading to the remote GPU setup running larger models like gemma-4-12b through LM Studio.\n\nNow I'm building out the CLI tool itself. I'll need to probe the hardware using PowerShell CIM queries to detect the CPU, RAM, GPUs, and identify the NPU by checking for \"Ryzen AI\" in the CPU name, plus probe the LAN endpoint for available models. Then I'll harvest model information by parsing the governance logs for lineage events and pulling from the workspace manifests, runs, and the dashboard execution register which tracks models and token counts. For dependencies, I'll scan package.json files and any Python requirements files or docker-compose configs. Finally, I'll query the graph database schema to get node labels, relationship types, and storage metrics across the workspace.\n\nI'm also adding code statistics by querying the CodeEntity nodes to count types and find the top classes by method count using the CODE_REL edges, plus tracking DEPENDS_ON relationships for component diagrams. Then I'll parse the governance logs for the latest completed swarm run to extract the task sequence showing the flow from operator through CLI to swarm to LMStudio to Neo4j. The diagrams section will generate mermaid strings for C4 context and container views.\n\nSticking with C4Context syntax since it's legitimate mermaid code and GitHub supports it. I'll also create usecase, class, sequence, and BPMN diagrams, plus entity-relationship and data model visualizations showing conceptual, logical, and physical layers with storage metrics. The deployment diagram will show the local setup with NPU/iGPU and LAN-connected eGPU nodes with their services and ports.\n\nFor the assemble phase, I'm reading the narrative file if it exists from a prior swarm run, otherwise using placeholders, then weaving everything together and writing the output. I'm also setting up observability to emit governance events tracking task metadata updates and the growing audit log per phase, with graceful handling for import failures. The audit module uses a relative workspace path, so the CLI needs to enforce the correct working directory so events land in the right governance log. I'm adding a `--run-swarm` flag that launches the CLI on the epic manifest between evidence and assemble phases, plus `--skip-swarm` for deterministic-only runs and `--narrative` to incorporate existing swarm output.\n\nWriting the file now...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":340003,"output_tokens":13750,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":489,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13750,"cache_read_input_tokens":340003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":489},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cd7MMnvLUDcWPRDGxKSP5","type":"assistant","uuid":"453e5055-51da-411b-8192-94a5540823ed","timestamp":"2026-07-17T08:57:33.803Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime","sessionId":"819e8a27-efc3-4128-b1f7-aa2f2dc4c806","version":"2.1.209","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
